// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 14-control-flow
// facility: rule.control.flow-analysis (`¬clash` at a place rooted at `*q`, D-0071; D-0219, CHG-0258); conf.read-through-reborrowed-reference
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// `r2` borrows `*r` exclusively and is used afterwards; reading `*r` in
// between conflicts with it. The discharge table refutes an access at a
// place rooted at `*q` when an overlapping, non-permitted
// `deriv(·, *q.·, ·)` is T, for a read as for a write. Both
// implementations refuted the write and left the read to the run, where
// it faulted; the model of D-0219 found the difference.

import std;

fn main()
{
    i32 y = 2;
    auto r = &mut y;
    auto r2 = &mut *r;
    i32 z = *r;
    *r2 = z + 1;
}
